/// Where a record came from. The distinction is load-bearing: a seeded
/// demonstration company and a company found this morning in a public permit
/// record look identical once they are rows in the same table, and acting on
/// the first is wasted work.
enum DataOrigin {
  /// Retrieved from a live external source by a connector.
  LIVE_DISCOVERY
  /// Supplied by the operator via CSV import.
  IMPORTED
  /// Entered by hand in the interface.
  MANUAL
  /// Created by the demonstration seed. Fabricated.
  SEED_DEMO
}

/// What a lead is to us, which is not the same as what the company is. The
/// same facilities-management firm is a buyer for janitorial supply and a
/// contractor looking for subcontractors, depending on the signal.
enum LeadRole {
  BUYER
  PROVIDER
  SUPPLIER
  PARTNER
  CONTRACTOR
  SUBCONTRACTOR
  UNKNOWN
}

/// Where a record sits between "this company exists" and "someone is buying".
///
/// The distinction this enum exists to enforce: a directory listing proves an
/// organisation exists and may fit the target profile. It does not prove any
/// intent to buy anything. Those were previously the same state, which is how a
/// gym that has never heard of us reached 88 points.
/// How much evidence exists that this account needs something *now*.
///
/// Separate from `LeadStage`, which tracks how far a hypothesis has been
/// worked. A record can sit in OPPORTUNITY_HYPOTHESIS forever at Tier D and a
/// brand-new Tier A record deserves attention before any of them. The two axes
/// answer different questions: the stage says what we have done, the tier says
/// what the world has done.
enum LeadTier {
  /// Direct evidence of a current commercial requirement — an open
  /// solicitation, an inbound request, a buyer actively sourcing vendors.
  ACTIVE_DEMAND
  /// No explicit request, but a dated event that usually creates need now:
  /// a permit, an award, a facility opening, an expansion.
  STRONG_TRIGGER
  /// Fits a pattern that has produced work before, with no current trigger.
  /// Campaign material. Must not compete with A or B for attention.
  PREDICTED_NEED
  /// Firmographic fit only — a directory or registry listing. Stored cheaply,
  /// kept out of the active pipeline. Most discovered records are this.
  DIRECTORY_PROSPECT
  /// Failed a rejection rule. Searchable, never surfaced as work.
  REJECTED
}

enum LeadStage {
  /// The organisation exists and a source vouches for it. Nothing more.
  DISCOVERED_ACCOUNT
  /// We think a named path might apply. Our idea, not their statement.
  OPPORTUNITY_HYPOTHESIS
  /// A dated external event suggests they may be buying.
  INTENT_DETECTED
  /// Need, decision-maker, timing, fit and next step are all established.
  QUALIFIED_LEAD
  /// Being actively worked as a deal.
  ACTIVE_OPPORTUNITY
  DISQUALIFIED
  NURTURE
}

/// Who is asserting a thing. Kept apart everywhere, because a source saying a
/// clinic exists, us guessing it needs cleaning, and a caller confirming it
/// does are three different degrees of truth that were being displayed
/// identically.
enum AssertionTier {
  /// Stated by the external source itself.
  SOURCE_FACT
  /// Derived by this system. A guess, however reasonable.
  SYSTEM_INFERENCE
  /// Confirmed by a person, usually on a call.
  USER_CONFIRMED
}

